<resources>
    <!--
      The brand, for the frame Android draws BEFORE JavaScript exists.

      Without this the launcher shows a white sheet for the second or so it
      takes to start the runtime, and the app appears to flash before it opens.
      The colour has to be duplicated here because a native resource cannot
      read `src/theme/tokens.ts` — see `src/common/brand.ts` for the rest of
      what a rename has to touch.

      LEAF GREEN, NOT EMBER ORANGE, and that was a real bug rather than a
      preference. This app has two palettes and `ThemeProvider` decides which
      side wears which: shopping is leaf, working is ember. Android cannot ask
      — this frame is painted before the process exists, let alone the store —
      so it has to be painted for the answer that is true for almost everybody
      and is what the store says from its first frame: customer.

      It was #E94E00. A shopper tapped an orange icon, waited behind an orange
      sheet and arrived in a green app.
    -->
    <color name="brand">#557F1D</color>
    <!--
      The launcher icon's ground. The same brand orange, named separately
      because it is read by `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` and a colour
      the LAUNCHER holds is not the same fact as the colour the splash frame
      holds — one of them can change without the other.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#557F1D</color>
    <color name="brand_dark">#456B14</color>
</resources>
